        ' ‘Our entry to practical and moral philosophy is the cosmic safehold, and [y]our key [to it] is
          the question, “To what end?”’  [So {maybe} including the reader to whom I might pose questions,
          or better, to whom I might give answers, the roles being reversed and I becoming|being
          convinced of the reader’s argument.]  Yet clarity above all, and here apropos of the metaphor:
          ‘I {could hardly|not}|cannot contemplate the prospect of entering the safehold without [asking]
          that question, nor make headway in[to] the philosophy without {insisting on a valid} |
          {[contemplating] the prospect of an} answer [to it] [*in that context*].’
